WEBVTT

00:24.192 --> 00:26.760
...15 minutes out,
we're still focusing.

00:28.496 --> 00:29.997
Can someone get me
the drop count?

00:31.299 --> 00:32.800
Okay. Good to go.

00:32.833 --> 00:35.002
We've got 60%.

00:35.035 --> 00:36.770
Copy that.

00:38.206 --> 00:40.141
We're doing a runner.
Make sure Paper Boi...

00:41.642 --> 00:43.977
And could you get rid of
all the ginger ale in there?

00:44.011 --> 00:45.613
Why?

00:47.115 --> 00:48.716
We asked for "ginger beer,"
not "ginger ale."

00:48.782 --> 00:50.218
Okay, I'm on it.

00:53.821 --> 00:55.689
Eyes on Paper Boi?

00:57.024 --> 00:58.992
Guys, eyes on Paper Boi?

01:00.661 --> 01:02.963
Niggas. Man...

01:02.996 --> 01:04.732
The hell is-- Is that a map?

01:04.798 --> 01:06.834
Uh, this is
an original blueprint

01:06.834 --> 01:08.802
of the building we're in.

01:08.836 --> 01:10.804
There's about f-four...
five rooms

01:10.838 --> 01:13.907
that I think are not on file.

01:13.974 --> 01:16.210
I smell adventure.

01:16.244 --> 01:17.845
Yes.

01:17.878 --> 01:19.713
Nigga, why you even-- Never
mind, man. I ain't doing it.

01:19.747 --> 01:21.915
Oh, man, they say this place
is, like, haunted.

01:21.982 --> 01:24.084
There's a lot of creepy,
unexplained events.

01:24.152 --> 01:25.853
Look, as long as it ain't
another Milwaukee,

01:25.886 --> 01:26.987
man, I'm cool.

01:27.020 --> 01:28.856
Mm. Are you talking
about the raid?

01:28.889 --> 01:31.559
I told you, man,
that was a ghost I saw.

01:31.592 --> 01:33.194
- Nigga, that was
your reflection.
- Hey, man.

01:33.194 --> 01:34.395
- Hey, what's going on?

01:34.428 --> 01:37.064
Yo, Al, Al, you trying to hit
a strip club after the show?

01:39.267 --> 01:41.068
- Oh, no!
- A strip club? Hell no.

01:41.101 --> 01:43.671
- No more European strip clubs,
all right, man?
- I heard that.

01:43.704 --> 01:45.339
It's 100 pounds to get in,

01:45.373 --> 01:47.040
and, uh,
we don't have any titties.

01:49.042 --> 01:50.678
Sprinkle me, milord.
- Sprinkle me.

01:50.711 --> 01:52.913
- Oh, please, make it rain
all over me.
- Make it rain.

01:52.946 --> 01:55.015
- Look at me trying
to clap my ass together...
- Make it rain.

01:55.048 --> 01:57.685
...but I can't find it, so...
Is it hot?

01:57.718 --> 01:58.952
Meet and greet.

01:59.019 --> 02:01.789
The kid from
the Dream Foundation.

02:01.855 --> 02:04.225
For sure, man. All right.

02:08.896 --> 02:11.031
- Hey, what's going on,
little man?
- Hello.

02:11.064 --> 02:12.933
This is Marvy.

02:12.966 --> 02:15.035
- What's that?
- Our evening plans.

02:43.897 --> 02:46.267
- Hi.
- One minute.

02:46.267 --> 02:47.935
It's me again.

02:47.968 --> 02:49.803
You're gonna be seeing a lot
of me. I'm gonna be in and out.

02:49.837 --> 02:52.840
Yeah, I know, I know,
I just need to check, you know?

02:52.906 --> 02:54.608
It's my job.

02:57.645 --> 03:00.248
- Okay. You're good to go.
- Thanks.

03:02.149 --> 03:04.952
Sorry, guys.
Uh, where were we? Um...

03:04.952 --> 03:07.187
Yeah, check the barricade,

03:07.255 --> 03:09.790
no flash photography
for the first three songs.

03:09.790 --> 03:11.425
I'm seeing a lot of people
walking around here;

03:11.459 --> 03:14.862
make sure people can't just
walk in on him...

03:31.178 --> 03:32.946
Hold that up.
Oh, there you go.

03:32.980 --> 03:35.816
Hey, guys. Hope you enjoyed
your time with Paper Boi,

03:35.816 --> 03:37.651
but, uh, he needs to get ready
for the show.

03:37.685 --> 03:39.953
There's a man outside
who'll escort you to your seats.

03:39.987 --> 03:42.656
You want
to take this with you?

03:42.690 --> 03:43.991
All right. There you go.

03:43.991 --> 03:45.125
All right,
y'all take it easy, man.

03:45.158 --> 03:47.227
All right.

03:50.230 --> 03:52.666
- Show in 30.
- All right.

03:52.700 --> 03:54.668
- Hey, you got my, um...
- Here you go.

03:54.702 --> 03:56.036
Cool.

04:01.008 --> 04:02.976
Oh, man,
can you get me a...

04:03.010 --> 04:05.145
Yeah, there's a ginger beer
on stage.

04:05.178 --> 04:07.014
It's right next to your water.
You were saying you were feeling

04:07.014 --> 04:09.016
"musty" on the way over here,
that means you're dehydrated.

04:09.049 --> 04:10.884
You should really drink
more water, but, yeah,

04:10.918 --> 04:12.219
the ginger beer's there.

04:12.252 --> 04:13.987
Okay.

04:17.257 --> 04:18.692
Hey, man, how you been?

04:20.060 --> 04:22.095
- Huh?
- How you been, man?

04:22.162 --> 04:23.864
Oh.

04:23.864 --> 04:25.032
Good, good.

04:25.032 --> 04:26.099
- Yeah?
- Yeah.

04:26.166 --> 04:27.935
Man, 'cause...

04:28.001 --> 04:29.937
...you seem busy
all the time, bruh.

04:30.003 --> 04:32.373
Yeah.

04:32.406 --> 04:34.207
But busy's good, you know?

04:34.207 --> 04:35.776
Yeah. Yep.

04:37.010 --> 04:39.279
All right, guys.

04:39.347 --> 04:42.082
Guys, I'm getting talkback
at the front of house.

04:42.115 --> 04:44.885
Can you check the patch?

04:44.918 --> 04:46.354
Turn the mic off.

04:55.796 --> 04:58.899
- cheering)

05:00.033 --> 05:02.536
Paper Boi! Paper Boi!

05:02.570 --> 05:05.105
- All right, give it up.
- All right, all right,
all right.

05:05.138 --> 05:07.975
Rap gods, for I am not
accustomed to prayer,

05:08.041 --> 05:10.043
bear with me.
I'd like to thank you

05:10.077 --> 05:12.145
for every life
that's here with me.

05:13.447 --> 05:15.115
- You shall bestow...
- Hell yeah.

05:15.148 --> 05:17.050
- ...Alfred with the energy
on to show.
- Yeah, man. Yeah!

05:17.084 --> 05:18.486
- Let's go!
- All right, shake.

05:18.552 --> 05:20.954
- He's here!

05:20.988 --> 05:24.091
Paper Boi! Come on!

05:24.091 --> 05:26.827
Whoo! Yeah!

05:26.894 --> 05:29.997
- Whoo-hoo-hoo!
- Hey!

05:31.565 --> 05:33.834
Get the fuck off the stage.

05:33.901 --> 05:36.770
Paper Boi!
Paper Boi! Paper Boi!

05:36.804 --> 05:37.971
Man, who the fuck is that?

05:38.005 --> 05:40.974
Paper Boi! Paper Boi!

05:41.008 --> 05:42.943
We'll deal with it
after the show.

05:42.976 --> 05:45.078
- Start the show?
- Good luck.

06:20.013 --> 06:22.983
I did not know you were poppin'
like that in Budapest.

06:23.016 --> 06:26.153
Might have to add this stop
to the next tour.

06:26.153 --> 06:27.320
What y'all looking for?

06:27.354 --> 06:29.322
Just tried again.
Went to voice mail.

06:29.356 --> 06:31.058
- Fucking phone?
- Yeah.

06:31.124 --> 06:32.960
Man, we need
to hurry up and find this.

06:32.993 --> 06:34.227
We still have
our map adventure to go on.

06:34.294 --> 06:36.363
Hey, man, I got back from
my set, my shit was gone.

06:36.396 --> 06:37.998
The one in the gold case?

06:37.998 --> 06:39.867
When was the last time
you had it?

06:39.900 --> 06:42.335
Man, it was out on the dock,
and then, uh...

06:42.335 --> 06:45.405
I came back in for the meet
and greet with that cancer kid.

06:45.473 --> 06:47.541
- And you didn't have it after?
- No, man.

06:48.676 --> 06:51.178
No, man.

06:51.178 --> 06:53.380
He wouldn't do that.

06:53.413 --> 06:55.516
There was something weird
about that kid, man.

06:55.549 --> 06:58.085
Uh, wait,
that dude is a fan, man.

06:58.151 --> 07:00.020
Imagine if you had your
favorite celebrity phone.

07:00.020 --> 07:01.922
Shit, man! Is he still here?

07:01.989 --> 07:03.256
Hold on.

07:03.323 --> 07:05.493
Yeah, does anybody
have eyes on the, uh,

07:05.526 --> 07:07.495
VIPs from the meet and greet?

07:07.528 --> 07:09.062
I think he's currently
being rushed

07:09.096 --> 07:10.564
out of the building.

07:10.598 --> 07:13.100
- Why?
- The paramedics were called in.

07:13.166 --> 07:15.368
He said he was having
a cancer attack.

07:15.402 --> 07:17.370
Cancer att... No.

07:17.370 --> 07:19.172
Hey. Hey, hey, hey, man, wa--

07:19.206 --> 07:21.174
I'm telling you,
if we just stick to...

07:21.208 --> 07:23.343
- Not now, man, not now.
- Ah... damn.

07:25.178 --> 07:26.880
Hey, hey!

07:26.914 --> 07:29.683
- I need to talk to that kid.
- What?

07:29.717 --> 07:30.884
No.

07:30.918 --> 07:33.220
If it is for Paper Boi,

07:33.220 --> 07:34.688
I want to help.

07:34.722 --> 07:37.057
- Marvy, I don't think...
- Mom.

07:37.090 --> 07:38.559
I need to do this.

07:38.559 --> 07:41.294
What does Paper Boi need?

07:51.471 --> 07:52.940
Um...

08:00.380 --> 08:01.982
Hey.

08:02.049 --> 08:04.417
- What are you doing?
- Get away from my son!

08:04.417 --> 08:06.419
Boo!

08:06.453 --> 08:09.590
Sorry. Thought he had a phone,
thought he had a phone.

08:11.592 --> 08:13.961
Hey, you find him?

08:13.994 --> 08:16.263
- He didn't take it.
- Man, how you know
he ain't take it?

08:16.296 --> 08:19.499
- What you do? You just ask...
- Believe me, he didn't have it.

08:19.567 --> 08:21.501
I could've told you
that boy didn't take that phone.

08:21.569 --> 08:23.336
Nigga, you the one... Whatever.

08:23.403 --> 08:25.238
Man, fuck, man.
I need that phone, Earn.

08:25.272 --> 08:27.575
It's just a phone, man.

08:27.608 --> 08:29.142
Look, I...

08:29.176 --> 08:31.444
I can have a runner get one
in the morning for you.

08:31.444 --> 08:33.013
Man, shit.

08:33.080 --> 08:35.583
I know this is
a very memorial vibe,

08:35.616 --> 08:37.651
but, uh, we can make
the whole situation

08:37.685 --> 08:39.286
a little bit better
if we just...

08:39.286 --> 08:41.288
Hey, look, it ain't even
about the phone, man.

08:41.321 --> 08:43.023
It's about the shit
that's on the phone.

08:43.090 --> 08:45.993
- iCloud?
- No, we don't do iCloud.

08:46.026 --> 08:48.428
No, yeah, exactly.
I'd have my shit backed up, too,

08:48.461 --> 08:50.297
if it wasn't for
conspiracy Jones over here.

08:52.099 --> 08:53.701
Who could've taken that phone?

08:55.535 --> 08:58.005
What about that runner guy?

08:58.038 --> 09:02.542
I think he was a runner, right?
That kid in the blue jacket?

09:02.610 --> 09:05.112
The super unprofessional
stage manager.

09:05.145 --> 09:08.015
That nigga that
was on the stage?

09:08.048 --> 09:10.150
Oh, I thought that dude
was the caterer.

09:16.790 --> 09:18.626
Oh, hey, buds.

09:18.659 --> 09:21.995
Good gig.

09:22.029 --> 09:23.631
You ready to settle up?

09:23.664 --> 09:27.034
Yeah, Folk, soon. Um, can I talk
to that stage manager?

09:27.067 --> 09:28.568
The stage manager?
He wasn't here today.

09:28.636 --> 09:30.570
I was covering for him.

09:30.638 --> 09:32.305
Then who was that guy?

09:32.339 --> 09:34.642
What guy?

09:34.675 --> 09:36.543
The guy who was...

09:36.576 --> 09:39.179
He had crazy brown hair,
he was kind of young,

09:39.179 --> 09:42.349
he was going around
asking people stuff...

09:42.382 --> 09:43.583
He had a blue jacket.

09:47.821 --> 09:50.090
- Oh, you talking about Wiley?
- Who?

09:50.157 --> 09:51.725
Yeah, Wi--
Blue jacket, brown hair.

09:51.759 --> 09:53.226
Yeah, Wiley. That's my nephew.

09:53.260 --> 09:54.695
- Your nephew?
- Yeah.

09:54.695 --> 09:58.365
He was here for a meeting
with the rigger about a job.

09:58.365 --> 10:00.701
Okay, well, Al had his phone
stolen. We need to talk to him.

10:00.701 --> 10:04.537
Really? That's very unfortunate.

10:04.571 --> 10:06.273
You don't think
Wiley took it, do you?

10:06.339 --> 10:08.075
Well, he was backstage
all night.

10:08.108 --> 10:10.277
Eh... I'm sure
he didn't take it.

10:11.679 --> 10:13.413
Well, I'm not saying he did,

10:13.446 --> 10:15.716
I'm just saying
we'd like to talk to him.

10:15.749 --> 10:16.850
Where is he?

10:16.884 --> 10:19.219
I don't know.

10:20.553 --> 10:23.390
Well... text him.
Can you text him?

10:23.390 --> 10:25.726
I don't have his number.

10:25.726 --> 10:27.427
You don't have
your nephew's phone number?

10:27.460 --> 10:29.562
No.

10:29.596 --> 10:33.233
I have his father's number, but
it is too late to call him now.

10:33.233 --> 10:34.534
Well, it's an emergency.

10:34.567 --> 10:37.237
An artist at your venue
had something stolen.

10:37.237 --> 10:39.539
The rigger has his number.

10:39.572 --> 10:40.808
I will get the number
from the rigger.

10:40.874 --> 10:42.275
Okay, I'll come with you.

10:42.309 --> 10:44.377
- What, you want it now?
- Yes.

11:04.231 --> 11:05.833
Old boy doesn't even work here.

11:05.899 --> 11:08.168
- Man, he don't work--
Then how the fuck...
- He's Folk's nephew.

11:08.235 --> 11:10.804
He was here for an interview,
but he left.

11:10.838 --> 11:12.806
This is his resume.
We got his info.

11:12.840 --> 11:14.607
Man, call this fucker right now.

11:14.641 --> 11:16.744
Hell yeah, and put that shit
on speakerphone, man.

11:21.815 --> 11:24.251
- Shit.

11:26.619 --> 11:27.788
Hello?

11:27.821 --> 11:31.458
Hey, uh, is this Wiley?

11:31.458 --> 11:32.826
Uh, as far as I know.

11:32.860 --> 11:36.196
Hi, this is, uh, Earn,
Paper Boi's manager.

11:36.263 --> 11:38.598
We spoke earlier today
at the show.

11:38.631 --> 11:40.300
Show?

11:40.300 --> 11:44.171
The-the Paper Boi concert.

11:44.204 --> 11:47.440
Oh...
Uh, the rap presentation.

11:47.474 --> 11:49.676
Yes. How can I help you?

11:49.709 --> 11:50.944
Yeah, well, you disappeared.

11:50.978 --> 11:53.480
Didn't you want
to meet Paper Boi?

11:53.480 --> 11:56.950
Yeah, but he seemed, uh, busy.
Yeah, busy.

11:56.984 --> 11:59.319
Well, he wanted to meet you.
We wanted to know if you,

11:59.352 --> 12:01.388
you know, live near the venue.

12:01.454 --> 12:06.459
You're, uh, you're calling
up fans randomly

12:06.493 --> 12:08.228
to invite them to meet you.

12:08.295 --> 12:10.463
- I feel like there's
an ulterior motive.
- No, no...

12:10.497 --> 12:12.332
Listen, man, we're done
playing with you, yeah?

12:12.365 --> 12:13.867
Do you know who you're
fucking with?

12:13.901 --> 12:16.203
- Socks.
- Keep playing
with Team Paper Boi, yeah,

12:16.236 --> 12:17.737
we're plugged in down here, man.

12:17.805 --> 12:19.672
Mob shit. Yeah?

12:19.706 --> 12:21.842
Like I'm the white
Liam Neeson, bruv.

12:21.875 --> 12:24.711
I will track you down,
and I will fucking bury you

12:24.744 --> 12:27.747
if you're not back here
in 15 minutes, phone in hand!

12:29.216 --> 12:30.583
Bring the fucking phone back,

12:30.650 --> 12:32.485
or we'll fucking kill you!

12:32.519 --> 12:35.522
What is this? What the fuck
is wrong with you, nigga?

12:37.590 --> 12:39.426
Hey, yo, man, hey.
What's going on, man?

12:39.492 --> 12:40.994
It's Paper Boi right here.

12:41.028 --> 12:43.831
We ain't gonna kill you, man.
We just, we just want to talk.

12:43.864 --> 12:45.765
That man said
you were going to kill me.

12:45.833 --> 12:48.001
Yeah, I know. I know, I know,

12:48.035 --> 12:50.337
but he, uh, he was
just playing, man. Hey,

12:50.370 --> 12:52.505
how about this, man, you-- if
you far-- Are you far from here?

12:52.539 --> 12:54.341
Whatever. Hey, man,
come back to the venue,

12:54.374 --> 12:56.009
I'll be here to meet you.
Call your uncle.

12:56.043 --> 12:59.512
I swear it's legit, for real.

12:59.546 --> 13:02.850
- Wiley?

13:02.883 --> 13:05.886
- What the hell, Socks?
- Look, I'm sorry, man.

13:05.919 --> 13:07.855
He's full of shit.
He's got that phone.

13:07.888 --> 13:09.756
Yeah. We knew that,

13:09.789 --> 13:11.758
but we need him
to come back here.

13:13.726 --> 13:15.762
- White Liam Neeson?
- Like, what the fu--

13:15.795 --> 13:17.630
That don't even make
no fucking sense, Socks, huh?

13:17.697 --> 13:19.532
Are you thinking
of Samuel L. Jackson?

13:19.566 --> 13:20.767
- Yeah, who are you
thinking about, man?
- What's wrong with you?

13:20.800 --> 13:23.403
Fucking Liam Neeson's
already fucking white!

13:34.381 --> 13:37.550
This is not how my night
was supposed to go, man.

13:37.584 --> 13:38.919
Yeah.

13:38.952 --> 13:40.954
Mine, either.

13:40.988 --> 13:42.990
Yo, he came back.

13:43.056 --> 13:45.258
Oh, shit.

13:53.901 --> 13:56.003
- God!
- Hey, hey, hey, hey.

13:56.069 --> 13:57.770
You stay out here, okay?

13:57.804 --> 13:59.606
You too hot, all right?

13:59.606 --> 14:01.674
Uh, yeah.

14:02.943 --> 14:04.477
Breathe.

14:04.511 --> 14:06.579
Yeah, it's cool,
it's cool, it's cool.

14:10.083 --> 14:12.285
Fuck!

14:15.022 --> 14:16.623
H-Hello.

14:16.623 --> 14:17.824
Hi.

14:21.929 --> 14:24.965
How... how are you guys
enjoying Budapest?

14:24.998 --> 14:27.000
Let's just get to the point.

14:27.034 --> 14:29.602
You didn't happen to see a phone
while you were backstage

14:29.636 --> 14:31.471
- all day, did you?
- What kind of phone, iPhone?

14:31.504 --> 14:33.440
- Uh, Samsung?
- Doesn't matter...

14:33.473 --> 14:35.808
Dawg, you find a phone or not?

14:36.944 --> 14:38.545
No.

14:40.013 --> 14:42.015
No, I didn't.

14:42.049 --> 14:43.984
You know there's a "find
my phone" app that could--

14:44.017 --> 14:46.353
- Yeah, that could help.
- No, no, no,
we don't use that.

14:46.386 --> 14:48.521
That's how they track us,
you know better than that.

14:48.555 --> 14:50.323
- Come on now.
- Ah.

14:54.361 --> 14:56.896
Why were you backstage all day?

14:57.998 --> 15:00.333
Oh, I was waiting
for my interview.

15:00.367 --> 15:02.535
Then why'd you come back?

15:02.569 --> 15:04.637
I thought about what you said.

15:06.539 --> 15:08.575
I didn't want to miss
a chance to meet...

15:08.641 --> 15:10.743
...Paper Boi.

15:10.810 --> 15:14.414
I'm a long-time admirer of his.

15:17.917 --> 15:20.753
Well, Paper Boi has
a really early flight tomorrow.

15:20.820 --> 15:22.755
And if you know
where his phone is,

15:22.822 --> 15:24.391
it'd be really helpful.

15:24.424 --> 15:27.360
Is there something special
about this phone?

15:27.394 --> 15:30.030
Is that why you said you were
going to kill me?

15:30.063 --> 15:31.164
- What?

15:31.198 --> 15:33.066
N-No, we didn't say that.

15:33.100 --> 15:34.934
We... we're not gonna hurt you.

15:35.002 --> 15:37.537
If I died today,
people will assume you did it,

15:37.537 --> 15:39.039
I think.
They-the will.

15:39.039 --> 15:40.873
Nobody's gonna die, Wiley.

15:40.907 --> 15:43.743
We all have to die sometime.

15:45.012 --> 15:46.779
You know that?

15:47.780 --> 15:49.616
Maybe my end...

15:51.451 --> 15:53.520
...should come
at the hands of Paper Boi.

15:58.525 --> 16:00.560
This is funny.

16:00.560 --> 16:03.196
Meeting you like this,
I feel like I'm dreaming.

16:03.230 --> 16:06.799
Trust me, ain't nobody
dreaming this, dawg.

16:10.603 --> 16:12.639
What do you dream of?

16:14.907 --> 16:17.544
Box-top Chevys?

16:18.978 --> 16:21.748
Or kissing the thorn on a rose?

16:21.748 --> 16:24.917
Oh, it's sweet, but it hurts.

16:27.920 --> 16:30.557
It'd make you never want
to trust...

16:31.891 --> 16:34.727
...anything too beautiful

16:34.761 --> 16:36.929
again.

16:42.769 --> 16:44.671
Out.

16:52.645 --> 16:54.614
Listen, he's just scared.

16:54.647 --> 16:56.616
He's only 19.

16:56.649 --> 16:58.118
He's my nephew through marriage.

16:58.151 --> 17:00.153
So, what happened--
did he admit to it?

17:00.187 --> 17:03.190
- Not yet.
- Oh, damn it!
Piece of shit, man!

17:03.256 --> 17:05.792
Fuck!

17:05.792 --> 17:07.594
That was strange.

17:07.627 --> 17:10.630
Have y'all noticed he's blinking
every five seconds on the dot?

17:10.663 --> 17:13.166
What was that...
"box-top Chevy" shit?

17:13.200 --> 17:15.168
I don't know, but I think

17:15.202 --> 17:17.104
we might find out if we just go

17:17.137 --> 17:18.805
to this one place on the map.
I'm telling you...

17:18.805 --> 17:20.807
- We're not gonna do the map.
- I know.

17:20.840 --> 17:22.675
That was my dream car
in high school.

17:22.709 --> 17:24.544
Box-top Chevy.

17:26.045 --> 17:28.047
And what about that rose thing?

17:28.115 --> 17:30.950
You know, "nothing... trust
anything beautiful again"?

17:30.983 --> 17:32.819
I used to date this girl
in high school.

17:32.852 --> 17:35.522
My boy Pookie fucked her--
her name was Rose.

17:35.555 --> 17:37.657
Yeah, Pookie stayed fucking her.

17:37.657 --> 17:39.992
So...

17:40.026 --> 17:42.162
how'd he know any of that?

17:42.195 --> 17:44.797
I rapped about it
in some early shit.

17:44.831 --> 17:47.167
Never released it, though.

17:47.200 --> 17:50.170
It was on my phone.

17:53.206 --> 17:55.708
Good cop?

17:55.742 --> 17:57.677
Bad cop.

17:57.710 --> 18:00.547
Devastated cop.

18:00.580 --> 18:03.516
Oh, here they come. Okay.

18:08.188 --> 18:10.990
I got you something.

18:11.023 --> 18:12.992
Thank you.

18:13.025 --> 18:14.894
You're welcome.

18:14.927 --> 18:17.864
Listen, you're obviously a fan.

18:17.864 --> 18:20.833
And sometimes fans get excited.

18:20.867 --> 18:23.035
And, you know, it's possible

18:23.069 --> 18:25.071
you just took the phone
by accident,

18:25.104 --> 18:27.240
and maybe you're embarrassed
to tell us.

18:27.274 --> 18:29.108
- And that's fine, that happens--
- You don't have the same accent,

18:29.176 --> 18:31.844
you know, the same
southern dialect as Paper Boi.

18:33.079 --> 18:35.582
- Uh...
- Were you told
as a child "you talk white"?

18:35.615 --> 18:37.884
Sometimes.

18:37.917 --> 18:40.086
Must've made you feel separate.

18:42.222 --> 18:44.224
What does that have
to do with anything?

18:44.224 --> 18:45.925
Nothing, nothing.

18:47.059 --> 18:50.197
I think it's interesting
when people aren't allowed

18:50.230 --> 18:52.232
in the group.

18:53.600 --> 18:56.068
The universal group.

18:57.136 --> 18:59.206
To be "part of the team."

19:00.873 --> 19:02.942
You know,
people just want to be seen.

19:04.377 --> 19:06.913
Doesn't matter what for.

19:06.946 --> 19:08.781
Can I have a cigarette?

19:08.815 --> 19:10.883
Sure.

19:12.719 --> 19:14.721
Here.

19:15.722 --> 19:18.090
Cool, cool.

19:23.263 --> 19:25.632
Why do people smoke these?

19:25.665 --> 19:27.800
Yep, I'm done.
I'm gonna beat you right now!

19:27.834 --> 19:29.101
Wait, wait!

19:29.101 --> 19:30.903
I want my one phone call.

19:30.937 --> 19:32.939
This isn't jail, Wiley.

19:32.939 --> 19:35.107
You can call anyone at any time.

19:35.107 --> 19:36.776
Okay, um, I don't have a phone.

19:36.809 --> 19:38.645
Could you, could you call
a number for me?

19:38.678 --> 19:39.846
Yeah, yeah.

19:39.912 --> 19:41.748
So it's, um, it's 404...

19:44.251 --> 19:46.619
And that's my fucking number,
nigga! You got my fucking phone!

19:46.653 --> 19:48.288
- Give me my fucking phone,

19:48.288 --> 19:50.623
man, stop playing with me!

19:53.926 --> 19:56.162
When I'm nervous, my stomach
churns-- it's disgusting.

19:56.195 --> 19:58.197
I am sorry.

19:58.265 --> 20:00.700
- Please don't hurt me.
- Oh!

20:02.435 --> 20:04.837
Hey, he's just a scared kid.

20:04.871 --> 20:07.106
You're interrogating
a 19-year-old.

20:07.139 --> 20:09.309
I'm 32.

20:12.211 --> 20:14.281
Nah!

20:17.817 --> 20:19.952
That's not strange to you?

20:19.986 --> 20:22.455
He's not 32, no way.

20:22.489 --> 20:25.325
He's either 32
or he's lying about being 32.

20:25.358 --> 20:28.194
Both is strange behavior.

20:28.227 --> 20:29.862
Has it been so long?

20:29.896 --> 20:31.464
I-I saw him maybe 15 years ago.

20:31.498 --> 20:33.666
- That still doesn't make him 32.
- Wait, wait.

20:33.700 --> 20:35.868
- 15 years?
- Mm.

20:35.902 --> 20:37.470
This guy's a stranger to you.

20:37.504 --> 20:39.171
You don't know him at all.

20:39.205 --> 20:41.841
He's my nephew...
through marriage.

20:41.841 --> 20:43.476
Okay, googled his address.

20:43.510 --> 20:46.212
It's the fucking
Cirque du Soleil headquarters.

20:46.245 --> 20:48.014
He's toying with us.

20:48.047 --> 20:49.682
When was the last time
you actually saw him, man?

20:49.716 --> 20:52.685
I visited him at juvenile
offenders institute.

20:52.719 --> 20:54.354
So jail, kid jail.

20:54.387 --> 20:55.922
Okay, so he's in on it,
isn't he?

20:55.988 --> 20:57.324
Hey, hey, stop, man!
Chill out, man!

20:57.357 --> 20:59.492
Go cool your ass off, bruh.

20:59.526 --> 21:01.328
I'm so mad,
I could kill this ni...

21:01.361 --> 21:04.030
Oh, I'm so mad, man.

21:08.067 --> 21:09.736
He definitely stole it.

21:09.769 --> 21:12.705
Mm-hmm, but we ain't got
no proof.

21:12.739 --> 21:15.342
Well, he wants
to be close to you, so...

21:15.375 --> 21:18.277
maybe just get him to confess
and we try and record it?

21:24.183 --> 21:26.386
Socks almost said "nigga,"
right?

21:26.386 --> 21:28.054
- He almost called us that.
- Yeah, I heard that.

21:34.394 --> 21:36.963
Hey, Folk, man,
can I get you to, uh...?

21:46.072 --> 21:48.808
Uh, so how much longer do you
think you will have me detained?

21:48.875 --> 21:50.943
Ain't nobody detaining you, man.

21:50.977 --> 21:53.245
Okay, I-I made you a crane.

21:58.250 --> 22:01.754
Listen,
I know things haven't gone well.

22:02.555 --> 22:04.457
And I want to do things
the right way.

22:05.992 --> 22:07.326
I haven't been
completely honest,

22:07.394 --> 22:09.396
which is why you guys,
you guys, uh,

22:09.429 --> 22:11.163
you had to resort to this, uh,

22:11.230 --> 22:12.965
you know, this good cop,
bad cop scenario.

22:12.999 --> 22:15.502
Uh, at this point,
I think you're probably

22:15.568 --> 22:17.970
gonna try to, uh, record me.

22:18.004 --> 22:20.507
To get me to say something
incriminating, but, uh...

22:22.442 --> 22:24.577
Look, I...

22:24.611 --> 22:27.346
I don't think
you'll get what you want

22:27.414 --> 22:29.816
that way.

22:34.521 --> 22:37.457
Earn, let me talk to him, man.

22:37.490 --> 22:39.526
Check on Folk.

23:05.518 --> 23:07.554
You know, I haven't written
anything in about...

23:07.620 --> 23:10.457
seven months.

23:10.490 --> 23:13.993
Seven months, man, yeah.

23:15.161 --> 23:17.396
Like, I go to the studio,
or I lay in bed,

23:17.464 --> 23:19.466
and like... bah.

23:19.499 --> 23:21.834
Like, nothing comes out.

23:21.868 --> 23:23.836
I can't find the words.

23:23.870 --> 23:26.038
It's like I don't know

23:26.072 --> 23:28.508
what's bad or good anymore.

23:35.347 --> 23:38.250
You know, I was never really
into rapping, either.

23:38.317 --> 23:40.319
Not really.

23:40.352 --> 23:42.321
Yeah, I know, like...

23:42.354 --> 23:44.390
now it's what I do.

23:44.423 --> 23:47.193
It's all I do, really.

23:48.260 --> 23:51.097
And, you know, it's just, uh,

23:51.163 --> 23:54.066
too late
for me to do anything else.

23:55.367 --> 23:58.237
But tonight-- oh, man-- tonight
I was out there on the dock

23:58.270 --> 24:00.272
before the show and, uh...

24:00.339 --> 24:02.208
I finally heard it.

24:02.208 --> 24:04.376
I finally heard him-- my voice.

24:04.410 --> 24:06.879
I heard him, man,
loud and clear, like...

24:06.913 --> 24:09.348
He was singing this melody, man.

24:09.381 --> 24:11.450
He was singing this melody
like he was a kid on a bus.

24:11.518 --> 24:13.553
And I started singing with him,
and it was....

24:13.553 --> 24:15.888
it was...

24:19.726 --> 24:21.894
It was fun.

24:24.463 --> 24:26.533
And I recorded that
on the phone.

24:27.534 --> 24:30.036
See what I'm saying, like...?

24:33.139 --> 24:35.141
And if I don't...

24:36.142 --> 24:38.277
If I don't...

24:38.310 --> 24:40.379
get it back now, then, uh...

24:40.412 --> 24:43.215
I'm afraid I'm gonna lose it.

24:43.249 --> 24:45.552
Forever, so...

24:49.756 --> 24:51.724
I need that phone.

24:51.758 --> 24:54.093
Wiley, you know what I'm saying?
Like, I need that phone.

24:54.126 --> 24:56.495
So...

24:56.563 --> 24:58.598
did you take my phone?

25:04.170 --> 25:06.338
Did you know we share
a birthday?

25:07.740 --> 25:10.476
Hmm? April 28th.

25:10.509 --> 25:12.278
We're Tauruses.

25:14.013 --> 25:16.015
Thank you.

25:18.450 --> 25:20.419
He texted me to...

25:26.458 --> 25:29.295
I like music, but I wasn't
really that into making it.

25:29.328 --> 25:31.497
I was a lot like you.

25:31.530 --> 25:34.433
Uh, then a girl broke my heart

25:34.466 --> 25:36.468
in eighth grade--
her name was Rosie.

25:36.468 --> 25:39.471
My mom moved me
and my sister to Budapest.

25:39.471 --> 25:42.675
I was really, really, really

25:42.709 --> 25:45.011
lonely.

25:46.378 --> 25:48.615
But when I heard
The Postal Mixtape...

25:51.317 --> 25:53.319
...I felt the same.

25:55.354 --> 25:57.389
I didn't sympathize.

25:59.158 --> 26:01.160
I didn't empathize.

26:01.160 --> 26:03.562
I felt...

26:03.630 --> 26:05.665
the-the same.

26:07.199 --> 26:09.468
Um, so...

26:12.371 --> 26:14.406
...I-I wrote this.

27:47.767 --> 27:50.269
Thank you for seeing me.

27:51.804 --> 27:54.440
I hope you find your phone.

28:48.327 --> 28:50.362
Hey?

28:51.463 --> 28:53.332
Sorry about back there, man.

28:53.365 --> 28:55.701
Sometimes I just...

28:55.734 --> 28:58.470
you know?

28:58.504 --> 29:00.639
We're good, yeah?

29:00.672 --> 29:03.309
- It's cool, man.
